.TH TASLEEMAT 1 "October 2026" "Tasleemat v2.6.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tasleemat \- Bilingual (English & Arabic) PMO Operating System, Interactive TUI Workstation, MCP Server & Governance Auditor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tasleemat
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B tasleemat
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fICOMMAND_OPTIONS\fR] [\fIARGUMENTS\fR]
.br
.B tasleemat
[\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR | \fBhelp\fR] [\fISUBCOMMAND\fR]
.br
.B tasleemat
\fBdocs\fR [\fITOPIC\fR]
.br
.B tasleemat
\fBman\fR [\fICOMMAND\fR|\fITOPIC\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Tasleemat
(تسليمات) is an enterprise-grade, open-source Project Management Office (PMO) operating system and programmatic toolkit designed for Project Managers, PMO Directors, Business Leaders, and Autonomous AI Agents.
.PP
It provides 114 standardized, bilingual (English & Arabic) project management deliverables (228 synchronized bundles total) covering the entire project lifecycle across 8 phases (00 to 07). Each deliverable is structured into a 5-file bundle comprising Markdown Templates, Practitioner Guides, AI Prompt Schemas, Machine-Readable Schemas (Draft 2020-12 JSON & Frictionless CSV), and Production Examples.
.PP
Tasleemat is fully aligned with PMI PMBOK® (6th, 7th & 8th Edition ready), ISO 21500 / 21502 standards, Saudi Digital Government Authority (DGA) regulations, and the NIST AI Risk Management Framework (AI RMF).
.SH OFFLINE & AIRGAPPED ENVIRONMENTS
Tasleemat is designed with zero-telemetry architecture and 100% offline capability for mission-critical, classified, and airgapped environments:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBZero External Network Calls:\fR All 114 forms, 228 bilingual deliverables, Draft 2020-12 JSON schemas, Frictionless data packages, bilingual lexicons, and documentation pages are bundled directly inside the Python package wheel.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBOffline Wheel Installation:\fR Can be transferred via airgap media and installed with:
.nf
    pip install \-\-no\-index \-\-find\-links /path/to/wheels tasleemat
.fi
.IP \(bu 2
\fBOffline AI & LLM Inference:\fR Built-in support for local Ollama endpoints (http://localhost:11434), vLLM, custom private endpoints, and offline mock generation (\fB\-\-mock\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBOffline Schema Validation & Governance Auditing:\fR Validate project structures, verify deliverable completion, and calculate Stage-Gate readiness without internet connectivity.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBNative Terminal Workstation:\fR The interactive TUI (\fBtasleemat tui\fR) operates entirely within the terminal with real-time Arabic text shaping and zero web asset dependencies.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init [\-n \fINAME\fR] [\-c \fICODE\fR] [\-\-pm \fIPM\fR] [\-\-sponsor \fISPONSOR\fR] [\-t \fITIER\fR] [\-p \fIPACK\fR] [\-l \fILANG\fR] [\-o \fIOUT\fR]
Scaffold a complete, tailored PMO project workspace populated with 5-file deliverable bundles based on governance tier, methodology pack, and language.
.TP
.B audit [\fIPATH\fR] [\-t \fITIER\fR] [\-p \fIPACK\fR] [\-\-strict] [\-\-no\-schema] [\-\-json] [\-o \fIOUT\fR]
Audit and verify a project workspace against PMO governance tiers and 6 Stage-Gates. Computes Overall Completion %, Governance Score %, and Draft 2020-12 schema conformance.
.TP
.B docs [\fITOPIC\fR]
Browse offline documentation guides. Supported topics include: \fIairgap\fR, \fItiers\fR, \fIpacks\fR, \fIgates\fR, \fIeva\fR, \fImcp\fR, \fIcatalog\fR, \fIlexicon\fR, and \fIcli\fR. Run with no arguments to list all available topics.
.TP
.B man [\fICOMMAND\fR|\fITOPIC\fR]
Display formatted manual reference page with pager support.
.TP
.B list [\-l {\fIar\fR|\fIen\fR}]
List all 114 project management forms in the master catalog indexed by phase and code.
.TP
.B search \fIQUERY\fR [\-l {\fIar\fR|\fIen\fR}]
Search the bilingual catalog for matching form titles, keywords, or PMO form codes.
.TP
.B generate \-f \fIFORM\fR [\-n \fINOTES\fR] [\-l {\fIar\fR|\fIen\fR}] [\-p \fIPROVIDER\fR] [\-m \fIMODEL\fR] [\-k \fIKEY\fR] [\-o \fIOUT\fR] [\-\-mock]
Auto-fill PMO deliverables from raw project notes using LLM AI accounts or offline mock mode.
.TP
.B config [{\fIset\fR|\fIshow\fR}] [\-\-provider \fIPROVIDER\fR] [\-\-model \fIMODEL\fR] [\-\-key \fIKEY\fR] [\-\-endpoint \fIURL\fR]
Configure default LLM AI credentials securely stored at ~/.tasleemat/config.json.
.TP
.B tui [\-l {\fIar\fR|\fIen\fR}]
Launch the full-screen interactive Terminal User Interface (TUI) workstation.
.TP
.B mcp
Start the Model Context Protocol (MCP) server over stdio for AI agent orchestration (Cursor, Claude Desktop, Antigravity, OpenCode).
.TP
.B test [\-v]
Execute the automated test suite verifying forms, schemas, calculations, and CLI functionality.
.SH GOVERNANCE TIERS
.TP
.B Tier 1: Enterprise / Strategic
High-budget, high-complexity, or safety-critical initiatives. Mandates 35 to 50 deliverables and all 6 Stage-Gates.
.TP
.B Tier 2: Standard Enterprise
Standard projects requiring structured oversight without excessive bureaucracy. Mandates 18 to 25 deliverables.
.TP
.B Tier 3: Fast-Track / Lean
Agile spikes, internal tooling, or low-risk operational changes. Mandates 7 to 9 essential deliverables.
.SH METHODOLOGY PACKS
.TP
.B General / PMBOK
Comprehensive PMI PMBOK® aligned baseline practices.
.TP
.B Agile / Scrum
Iterative development, sprint backlogs, burn-up/down charts, and retrospective improvements.
.TP
.B AI Governance & Engineering
NIST AI RMF, ISO/IEC 42001, AI model cards, ethical impact assessments, and data bias checks.
.TP
.B Predictive / Waterfall
Formal sequential phases with strict baseline control.
.TP
.B Hybrid
Blends predictive governance and executive gates with iterative sprint-based execution.
.SH STAGE-GATES
.TP
.B Gate 0: Strategic Alignment & Mandate
Verifies organizational need and portfolio fit.
.TP
.B Gate 1: Business Case & Justification
Approves financial justification, benefits realization, and feasibility.
.TP
.B Gate 2: Project Charter Authorization
Formal authorization granting the Project Manager authority to commit resources.
.TP
.B Gate 3: Integrated Baseline Approval
Locks Scope, Schedule, Cost, Quality, and Risk baselines prior to major execution spend.
.TP
.B Gate 4: Operational Readiness
Confirms deliverable acceptance, transition plans, training, and operational handover.
.TP
.B Gate 5: Handover, Benefits Realization & Closeout
Final contractual acceptance, lessons learned archiving, and administrative project closure.
.SH EARNED VALUE ANALYSIS (EVA)
Tasleemat includes an exact mathematical EVA calculation engine:
.PP
.nf
  Planned Value (PV), Earned Value (EV), Actual Cost (AC), Budget at Completion (BAC)
  Cost Variance (CV)        = EV - AC
  Schedule Variance (SV)    = EV - PV
  Cost Performance (CPI)    = EV / AC
  Schedule Performance (SPI)= EV / PV
  Estimate at Completion    = BAC / CPI  (typical variances)
  Estimate to Complete      = EAC - AC
  Variance at Completion    = BAC - EAC
  To-Complete Index (TCPI)  = (BAC - EV) / (BAC - AC)
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B TASLEEMAT_HOME
Custom directory for configuration and workspace defaults (Default: ~/.tasleemat).
.TP
.B TASLEEMAT_OFFLINE
Set to 1 to force offline operation and suppress any network requests.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Set to 1 to disable ANSI terminal colors.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error, schema validation failure, or audit compliance violation in strict mode.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line syntax or argument parsing error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Scaffold a standard Arabic Agile workspace:
.PP
.nf
    tasleemat init \-\-tier 2 \-\-pack agile \-\-lang ar \-\-name 'منصة التحول الرقمي' \-\-code 'PRJ-2026-01'
.fi
.PP
Audit a project workspace in strict CI/CD mode with JSON output:
.PP
.nf
    tasleemat audit ./my_project \-\-tier 2 \-\-pack agile \-\-strict \-\-json \-o audit_report.json
.fi
.PP
Read the offline airgap operation guide:
.PP
.nf
    tasleemat docs airgap
.fi
.PP
Display the offline reference manual:
.PP
.nf
    tasleemat man
.fi
